  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Nickels (Three Thirteen). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Nickels (also known as Three Thirteen or 65) is a progressive Rummy-style card game played over 11 distinct rounds. The game starts with three cards dealt to each player and ends with thirteen cards in the final round. It is known for its shifting 'Wild Card' rule, where the rank corresponding to the number of cards dealt becomes wild for that specific round. It is a game of patience, set-building, and risk-management, where the goal is to have the lowest cumulative score.",
    objective: 'Have the lowest total penalty points at the end of 11 rounds.',
    gameplay: '1. Draw a card (from deck or discard).\n2. Form melds: Sets (3+ of a rank) or Runs (3+ of a suit in sequence).\n3. Discard one card to end the turn.\n4. **Going Out**: When a player can meld ALL their cards (using a final discard), everyone else has one last turn to improve their hand before scoring.',
    keyRules: [
      'Progressive rounds: 3 to 13 cards per round',
      'Form Sets (3+ same rank) or Runs (3+ same suit in sequence)',
      'Wild cards change each round (rank equals card count)',
      'Draw from deck or discard, then discard one card to end turn',
      'Going out: meld all cards; others get one last turn',
    ],
